# Purpose
Documents what every current closed dashboard-console guidance element does,
why it is helpful, how to use it, and the exact public-safe bubble copy.

# Dependencies
- `guidance-markers.md` defines the marker format and safety boundary.
- The authenticated dashboard's closed guidance vocabulary remains authoritative.

# Gotchas
- Curated aliases cover common human language; automatic exact keys cover every
  live native, disclosure, focusable, and declared-action element, including
  dynamically created controls. Internal anchors are normalized into the exact namespace.
- Keep target names synchronized with the live guidance tool schema.
- Keep marker messages plain text and no longer than 180 characters.
- Image-input instructions must never substitute a paperclip for the plus and Attach controls shown by the dashboard.
